course: dictionary
lesson: 2940
title: Dreary: grey, dull and gloomy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dreary is an adjective, so it describes a noun: a dreary day, dreary weather, dreary work. Its other forms are drearier, for comparing two things, and dreariest, for the most.
explain: Dreary means dull, grey and gloomy. A dreary day has no sun, a flat grey sky and rain, and it can make you feel a bit sad or bored. Writers use dreary to set a gloomy mood in a story.
explain: Dreary also describes things that are boring. A dreary job, book or talk has nothing exciting in it. Look at the clues around the word: grey and wet means weather, while nothing exciting means boring.
explain: Other places have their own words for the same idea. Grandad says «dreich», which means grey and wet, so it is a Scottish word for dreary. Context and a dictionary help you find the match.
fact: Dreary means dull, grey and making you feel sad or bored.
fact: Dreary describes weather, places and feelings, and it can also describe boring work.
fact: The comparison forms are drearier (more dreary) and dreariest (the most dreary).
fact: «Dreich» (Scotland) means dreary: a grey, wet day.
fact: Writers use dreary to set a gloomy mood, so look for it when a story feels sad or grey.
exercise: A dreary day has no sun, a grey sky and rain. What does dreary mean? | Bright and sunny | *Dull, grey and making you feel sad or bored | Very loud and busy | Frozen solid
exercise: Their talk was dreary, with nothing exciting in it. What does dreary mean here? | Very fast | Brightly coloured | *Boring, with nothing exciting | Funny and loud
exercise: Grandad says «dreich». What does it mean? | A big dinner | *Grey and wet, dreary | A hot, sunny day at the beach | A tiny dog
test: Which word means more dreary? | dreariest | drearing | *drearier | dearer
test: Which phrase describes boring work? | *A dreary job | A warm bath | A loud firework | A sunny beach
exam: Which description fits a dreary day best? | *Grey, wet and gloomy | Full of sun and laughter | Full of sparkling snow | Very windy and warm
